🌗 [I]Top shadow was so shy it only came out after you opened the drawer. It's had a pep talk and now shows up for work on time.[/I][/QUOTE]

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]💬 Community Notes[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Thank you[/B] to the reporter of [URL="https://github.com/denson9874/ExpressiveLauncher/issues/15"]#15[/URL] for the crash log that pinned down the restore crash.
[*][B]Still being worked on[/B] (see the 5.0.0 release notes for workarounds):
[*]Swiping up on a cover folder doesn't open it yet; tap still opens the cover app.
[*]The headphone battery card in At a Glance doesn't appear yet.
[*]Lowering Dock pages or Dock rows, or folding a foldable, can remove dock icons that no longer fit.
[*]The first setting you change after Home starts can restart Home a few times.
[*][B]Validation[/B]: 616 automated tests pass. The fixes were checked on Android 17 (QPR2) emulators, with and without Pro, and on an Android 12 emulator where the restore crash loop was reproduced on 5.0.2 and cleared by updating to 5.0.3 with the layout intact. 21,000 random monkey events ran with no crashes. Physical-device reports are very welcome.
[*][B]Developer Support[/B]: Expressive Pro is available as a one-time $4.99 activation. Every dollar directly funds our ongoing tooling and infrastructure expenses—including automated CI/CD servers, dedicated Android 17 testing devices/emulators, signing pipelines, and active continuous development—keeping Expressive fast, independent, and completely ad-free.

[/LIST]
[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]🧩 Release Riddle[/B][/SIZE]

[QUOTE][I]I'm pressed a thousand times a day, yet on Home I used to ignore the job you gave me. Since 5.0.3 I finally do what you asked. What am I?[/I][/QUOTE]

[SPOILER="Tap to reveal answer"][B]The Back button![/B] It's been waiting for its moment on Home for a long time. ↩️[/SPOILER]

